        "comments": "The assembly drMyrAqua2.hap1.1 is based on 139x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The species had been a allohexaploid in the past (6n = 42), but today it works as functional diploid. In every set of 6 chromosomes observed on the HiC map, we can see 3 chromosome pairs that look to recombine. The HAP1 file contain one curated copy of each sub genome. The order and orientation of the scaffolds on the centromeric region of Chromosome 1, 22.98 Mbp - 33.47 Mbp, are uncertain.",
